@startuml
title SysMon - LLM Server Instance State Diagram

[*] --> RuntimeCheck : Admin clicks Spawn

state RuntimeCheck
state Installing
state Configuring
state Validating
state Starting
state Running
state Failed
state Stopping
state Stopped

RuntimeCheck --> Installing : Ollama missing
RuntimeCheck --> Configuring : Ollama already available
Installing --> Configuring : installOllama() succeeds
Installing --> Failed : installOllama() fails

Configuring --> Validating : model repo and\nruntime parameters set

Validating --> Starting : fitsComputeGroup()\nand portAvailable()
Validating --> Failed : exceeds Compute Group\nor port in use

Starting --> Running : startOllamaServer() succeeds
Starting --> Failed : startOllamaServer() fails

Running --> Stopping : stopLLMServer() confirmed
Running --> Running : restartLLMServer()\n(stop then start)

Stopping --> Stopped : terminateProcess()
Stopping --> Running : Admin cancels stop

Failed --> [*]
Stopped --> [*]

note right of Running
  Instance registered in LLM console.
  Methods: ensureOllama, validateAgainstGroup,
  startOllamaServer, stopLLMServer,
  restartLLMServer, terminateProcess.
  Takes Compute Group as argument
  during Validating.
end note

@enduml
